WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.039
A content type defines a kind of content on your site, such as

00:00:05.039 --> 00:00:07.356
a page, a blog post, or an event.

00:00:07.356 --> 00:00:11.158
In this video, you create a type, add a part and fields to

00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:13.890
it, set their order, and create an item.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.520
Every content item belongs to a content type, such as a Page, a

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.214
Blog Post, or an Event.

00:00:24.214 --> 00:00:28.070
What an editor fills in for an item comes from the parts and

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.530
fields of its type.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.507
A part is a behavior that you attach to a type.

00:00:33.507 --> 00:00:37.890
The Title part, for example, gives every item of the type a title.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.019
A field holds a piece of data that you define, such as a

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:43.817
venue, a number, or a date.

00:00:43.817 --> 00:00:46.923
The fields you add to a type live in a part that is

00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:48.340
named like the type.

00:00:52.543 --> 00:00:56.975
In the admin menu, open Design, Content Definition, Content Types.

00:00:56.975 --> 00:01:01.713
The page lists every content type of the site, with its technical name.

00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:06.620
Each row has buttons to list items, edit the type, and delete it,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.314
and one to create an item when the type is Creatable.

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:16.580
Viewing types needs the View content types permission, and changing them needs Edit content types.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:18.703
The Administrator role has both.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:20.659
Let's select Create new type.

00:01:21.118 --> 00:01:26.523
Enter Event as the Display Name, which is the name that editors see on screens.

00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:29.448
The Technical Name fills in as you type.

00:01:29.924 --> 00:01:34.580
The technical name identifies the type, and it can't be changed later.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.358
It must start with a letter and contain no spaces or special characters,

00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:42.359
and a reserved or existing name is refused.

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:43.584
Select Create.

00:01:44.038 --> 00:01:48.661
Orchard Core confirms that the content type has been created, and opens the

00:01:48.661 --> 00:01:50.258
Add Parts page for it.

00:01:54.495 --> 00:01:57.884
The Add Parts page lists the parts that can be attached to the

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.977
type, most with a short description.

00:01:59.977 --> 00:02:03.415
Which parts appear depends on the features enabled on the site.

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:06.255
Let's tick Title, which adds a title to every item.

00:02:06.718 --> 00:02:09.920
Add Selected Parts appears once a part is ticked.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.926
The Add & Configure button on a row adds only that part, and opens its settings.

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:17.138
Let's select Add Selected Parts.

00:02:17.591 --> 00:02:19.728
The Edit Content Type page opens.

00:02:19.728 --> 00:02:23.289
At the top are the names and the settings of the type, such

00:02:23.289 --> 00:02:27.453
as Creatable and Listable, which are turned on when a type is created.

00:02:27.453 --> 00:02:29.371
A separate video covers them.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:34.197
Further down, under Parts, Title is listed with an Edit button, which opens

00:02:34.197 --> 00:02:38.884
the settings of the part, and a Remove button, which takes the part off the type.

00:02:43.094 --> 00:02:45.377
Under Fields, select Add Field.

00:02:45.377 --> 00:02:49.696
Enter Venue as the Display Name, and the Technical Name follows.

00:02:49.696 --> 00:02:53.584
A field stores a value for each content item of the type.

00:02:54.051 --> 00:02:58.273
Field Type lists the kinds of value a field can hold, such as

00:02:58.273 --> 00:03:01.613
Text Field, Numeric Field, and Date Time Field.

00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:05.331
Venue is plain text, so select Text Field, then Save.

00:03:05.791 --> 00:03:09.488
Save returns to the type, and Venue is listed under Fields.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.446
Under Parts, the part named Event appears too:

00:03:12.446 --> 00:03:16.371
its hint says that it contains the fields for the current type.

00:03:16.826 --> 00:03:19.334
Let's add Starts as a Date Time Field.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:23.666
This time, select Save & Configure, to open the settings of the field.

00:03:24.174 --> 00:03:27.325
The Technical Name of a field is read-only here.

00:03:27.325 --> 00:03:31.526
Tick Required, so that editors must fill the field in, and write a

00:03:31.526 --> 00:03:35.552
Hint, the help text that appears under the field in the editor.

00:03:35.552 --> 00:03:36.894
Then select Save.

00:03:37.345 --> 00:03:40.578
Back on the type, Starts is listed with Venue.

00:03:40.578 --> 00:03:43.252
Let's add a third field the same way:

00:03:43.252 --> 00:03:46.485
Capacity, as a Numeric Field, and select Save.

00:03:46.949 --> 00:03:51.140
Each field in the list has an Edit button, which reopens its settings,

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.559
and a Remove button, which takes the field off the type.

00:03:58.784 --> 00:04:02.631
Once the type is saved, the editor of an item shows its parts

00:04:02.631 --> 00:04:05.214
and fields in the order of these lists.

00:04:05.214 --> 00:04:09.004
Let's drag Starts above Venue, so that the date comes first.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:10.506
Select Save.

00:04:10.506 --> 00:04:14.402
It stores the order of the parts and of the fields, and returns

00:04:14.402 --> 00:04:16.209
to the Content Types page.

00:04:20.464 --> 00:04:24.286
The Content Types page lists Event, with its technical name.

00:04:24.286 --> 00:04:28.454
Select Create New Event to open the editor that the type produces.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:33.158
The editor shows the Title, then the fields in the order you set.

00:04:33.158 --> 00:04:37.943
Starts is marked with an asterisk, and the hint you wrote appears under it.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:42.504
Let's enter a title, a start, a venue, and a capacity.

00:04:42.504 --> 00:04:46.878
Save Draft stores a draft, and Publish publishes the item.

00:04:46.878 --> 00:04:48.313
Select Publish.

00:04:48.797 --> 00:04:52.275
Orchard Core confirms that the Event has been published.

00:04:52.275 --> 00:04:56.257
Select List Items on its row to see the item in the content list.

00:05:00.457 --> 00:05:01.256
To recap:

00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:05.360
create the type with its names, attach the parts that give it behavior,

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:09.837
add the fields that hold its values, and drag them into the order editors see.

00:05:11.837 --> 00:05:15.249
That's a content type, built from parts and fields in the admin.

00:05:15.249 --> 00:05:16.517
Thanks for watching.

